From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v0lumehi <aljic.zijad@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:21:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] front_mac: enter fullscreen once the app is active and the
 window is on the active Space, repeat a refused request once

A game opened from an app that is in fullscreen stayed a window. The request is now made when the app is active and the window is on the active Space, and repeated once when AppKit reports a refusal.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#665
Reason: A game started with DM_FULLSCREEN from the launcher's fullscreen console mode stays a window
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#219
---
 dm/host/front_mac.m          | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 docs/reference/frame-rate.md |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/front_mac.m b/dm/host/front_mac.m
index 3a83af0c..7671c20a 100644
--- a/dm/host/front_mac.m
+++ b/dm/host/front_mac.m
@@ -236,6 +236,13 @@ - (void)setFrameSize:(NSSize)s { [super setFrameSize:s]; [self fitDrawable]; }
 - (void)viewDidChangeBackingProperties { [super viewDidChangeBackingProperties]; [self fitDrawable]; }
 @end
 
+// The window's delegate: AppKit reports a refused fullscreen request only here (there is no notification for it)
+static void (^g_fs_failed)(void);
+@interface DmWinDelegate : NSObject <NSWindowDelegate> @end
+@implementation DmWinDelegate
+- (void)windowDidFailToEnterFullScreen:(NSWindow *)w { (void)w; if (g_fs_failed) g_fs_failed(); }
+@end
+
 typedef struct { void (*fn)(void); } guest_arg;
 static void *guest_tramp(void *p) {
     static char alt[65536];                       // The signal alternate stack is per thread; crash printing must also work on the guest thread
@@ -288,7 +295,25 @@ void front_run(void (*guest)(void)) {
         [wm addItemWithTitle:@"Enter Full Screen" action:@selector(toggleFullScreen:) keyEquivalent:@"f"].keyEquivalentModifierMask = NSEventModifierFlagControl | NSEventModifierFlagCommand;
         NSApp.mainMenu = bar;
         const char *fs = getenv("DM_FULLSCREEN");   // 1 (or any value but 0): start in fullscreen; 0, the settings window's Window, or unset: a window
-        if (fs && strcmp(fs, "0")) dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{ [win toggleFullScreen:nil]; });
+        if (fs && strcmp(fs, "0")) {
+            // A game opened from an app that is itself in fullscreen starts while macOS leaves that Space: a request made right away reaches a window that is not on the active Space
+            // or an app that is not active yet, and AppKit can refuse it (the game stayed a window). So the request waits for the app to be active with its window on the active Space (activation or
+            // Space change, whichever comes last), and a refused one is repeated once. It stops as soon as the player toggles fullscreen themselves
+            static DmWinDelegate *wd; wd = [DmWinDelegate new]; win.delegate = wd;
+            __block int want = 1, retried = 0;
+            void (^enter)(void) = ^{
+                if (!want || (win.styleMask & NSWindowStyleMaskFullScreen) || !NSApp.isActive || !win.isOnActiveSpace) return;
+                want = 0; [win toggleFullScreen:nil]; };
+            g_fs_failed = ^{
+                LOG("front end: fullscreen was refused (app active %d, window on the active Space %d)%s", NSApp.isActive, win.isOnActiveSpace, retried ? "" : ", asking once more");
+                if (retried) return;
+                retried = 1; want = 1; dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), enter); };
+            [NSNotificationCenter.defaultCenter addObserverForName:NSApplicationDidBecomeActiveNotification object:nil queue:nil usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) { (void)n; enter(); }];
+            [NSWorkspace.sharedWorkspace.notificationCenter addObserverForName:NSWorkspaceActiveSpaceDidChangeNotification object:nil queue:nil usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) { (void)n; enter(); }];
+            for (NSNotificationName nm in @[NSWindowWillEnterFullScreenNotification, NSWindowWillExitFullScreenNotification])
+                [NSNotificationCenter.defaultCenter addObserverForName:nm object:win queue:nil usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) { (void)n; want = 0; }];   // the player's own toggle (ours already cleared it)
+            dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), enter);
+        }
         for (NSNotificationName nm in @[GCControllerDidConnectNotification, GCControllerDidDisconnectNotification])
             [NSNotificationCenter.defaultCenter addObserverForName:nm object:nil queue:NSOperationQueue.mainQueue usingBlock:^(NSNotification *n) {
                 GCController *c = n.object; int conn = n.name == GCControllerDidConnectNotification;
diff --git a/docs/reference/frame-rate.md b/docs/reference/frame-rate.md
index 01e3d2f1..19e21153 100644
--- a/docs/reference/frame-rate.md
+++ b/docs/reference/frame-rate.md
@@ -202,6 +202,14 @@ Frame pacing: the host's frame step, engine frame limiters, present intervals an
 - **Check:** here (a built-in 120 Hz screen, a multiple of every link rate) a harness drove `front_mac.m` asked for 50 fps: no switch in the window, 120 → 50 Hz in fullscreen, 120 Hz again on leaving it, and 120 Hz after quitting in fullscreen; at 60 fps and with `DM_SCREEN_MATCH=0` nothing switched.
 - **Not checked:** the link's new range after a switch has not run here (Hades windowed and fullscreen paced at 60 as before).
 
+### A game opened from a fullscreen app stays a window
+
+- **Symptom:** a Mac game started with `DM_FULLSCREEN=1` from an app that is itself in fullscreen (the launcher's console mode) came up as a window. The reporter: "using a full screen app to launch another full-screen app will fail, it will automatically switch to windowed mode".
+- **Cause:** the launcher lives in its own fullscreen Space, so opening the game makes macOS leave that Space. `front_run` asked for fullscreen on the next run-loop turn, when the log of a test harness (two small apps, the second making the same request) shows the app active but its window not yet on the active Space (`isOnActiveSpace` 0, the Space change arriving 0.3 to 0.5 s later). AppKit drops a request made then and reports it only to the window delegate (`windowDidFailToEnterFullScreen:`, there is no notification). That the request is refused in that state is **open**: the harness took it every time, so the failure itself has not been reproduced here, only the state in which it is made.
+- **Fix:** `front_mac.m` `front_run` makes the request once the app is active and the window is on the active Space (`NSApplicationDidBecomeActiveNotification`, `NSWorkspaceActiveSpaceDidChangeNotification`, whichever comes last), repeats a refused one once (the `fullscreen was refused` line), and stops when the player toggles fullscreen first. `g_fullscreen` and `screen_match_apply` are unchanged. The alternative, a borderless screen-sized window with no Space of its own, would avoid the transition but give up native fullscreen, which `screen_match_apply` relies on.
+- **Found on:** the NX2Apple launcher's console mode (LNPANDY/NX2Apple), no game in particular.
+- **Not checked:** the refusal itself, and a game started through the real console mode.
+
 ### Frame latency 2 for the display link in fullscreen
 
 - **Symptom:** on a ProMotion built-in screen, only in fullscreen, the frame step went 1 → 2 → 3 vsyncs on frames costing 0.1–0.6 vsyncs (`3 late frames; cost 0.32 vsyncs`) and the game presented 15 frames a second; a window, or the screen set to a fixed 60 Hz, did not do it. The `DM_NVN_TSV` rows show presents shown one 120 Hz refresh late (`@pres_at_ms` − `@link_target_ms` = 8.3 ms) with a skipped tick after each (`@link_gap_ms` 33 ms), and `@link_lead_ms` about 16 ms against about 50 ms in a window.
